Link native dependencies against Arch's system shared libraries.

audiopus_sys: Arch ships no libopus.a, so switch the crate to its `dynamic`
feature, remove upstream's OPUS_NO_PKG setting to re-enable pkg-config, and
hand its build script LIBOPUS_LIB_DIR=/usr as a direct-link fallback. Together
these paths find the system shared library and avoid cmake-building vendored
Opus. The remaining cmake/msvc env keys stay in place, inert.

pcre2-sys: only offers pkg-config discovery, so flip upstream's
PCRE2_SYS_STATIC from 1 to 0 (0 is an explicit "not static", not merely unset)
and let it probe libpcre2-8 from /usr.

onig_sys: RUSTONIG_SYSTEM_LIBONIG=1 requires pkg-config to locate
Arch's `oniguruma` package and rejects a fallback to its vendored copy.

Hunks deliberately replace unique lines: upstream frequently churns
MODULE.bazel's comments and neighbouring env keys, while these anchors avoid
unrelated edits making the patch fail.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -244 +244 @@
-audiopus_sys = { version = "0.2.2", features = ["static"] }
+audiopus_sys = { version = "0.2.2", features = ["dynamic"] }
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -166 +166,2 @@
-        "OPUS_NO_PKG": "1",
+        # Fall back to Arch's shared /usr/lib/libopus.so if pkg-config fails.
+        "LIBOPUS_LIB_DIR": "/usr",
@@ -192 +192 @@
-    build_script_env = {"PCRE2_SYS_STATIC": "1"},
+    build_script_env = {"PCRE2_SYS_STATIC": "0"},
@@ -202 +204,7 @@
-use_repo(crate, "crates")
+# Link Arch's oniguruma through pkg-config.
+crate.annotation(
+    crate = "onig_sys",
+    build_script_env = {"RUSTONIG_SYSTEM_LIBONIG": "1"},
+)
+
+use_repo(crate, "crates")
